=== dis deletes the sentence under the cursor
ref:    motion.txt *is*
quote:  "\"inner sentence\", select [count] sentences"
given:  One two.  Th|ree four.  Five.
keys:   dis
expect: One two.  |  Five.
regs:   "" = "Three four."

=== das deletes the sentence and the white space after it
ref:    motion.txt *as*
quote:  "\"a sentence\", select [count] sentences"
given:  One two.  Th|ree four.  Five.
keys:   das
expect: One two.  |Five.
regs:   "" = "Three four.  "
undo:   One two.  |Three four.  Five.

=== das on the last sentence takes the white space before it
ref:    motion.txt *o_object-select*
quote:  If there is no white space after the object or when the cursor was in the white space before the object, the white space before the object is included.
given:  One two.  Th|ree four.
keys:   das
expect: One two|.
regs:   "" = "  Three four."

=== dis on the white space between sentences deletes the white space
ref:    motion.txt *o_object-select*
quote:  If the cursor was on white space, the operator applies to the white space.
given:  One two. |  Three.
keys:   dis
expect: One two.|Three.
regs:   "" = "   "

=== d2as deletes two sentences
ref:    motion.txt *as*
quote:  select [count] sentences
given:  |One.  Two.  Three.
keys:   d2as
expect: |Three.
regs:   "" = "One.  Two.  "

=== a sentence may end at ! or ?
ref:    motion.txt *sentence*
quote:  A sentence is defined as ending at a '.', '!' or '?' followed by either the end of a line, or by a space or tab.
given:  Why? Be|cause! Done.
keys:   dis
expect: Why? | Done.
regs:   "" = "Because!"

=== cis replaces the sentence
ref:    motion.txt *is*
quote:  select [count] sentences
given:  One. Tw|o. Three.
keys:   cisX.<Esc>
expect: One. X|. Three.
regs:   "" = "Two."
